    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 10th slate with a clear offensive ceiling anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier start, boasting an elite 0.469 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Quantrill, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** provides critical upside in our scarcest category\u2014stolen bases\u2014utilizing his elite speed profile against Greene. We are also leaning heavily into **Trea Turner** (69.64) at the top of the order, whose matchup against Flaherty is bolstered by a significant +10% order bonus. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our top speed threat, he carries a 35% rain risk; should his game be delayed, we are monitoring bench availability to ensure we don't bleed plate appearances in a tight Roto race.\n\nMid-tier value is derived from strategic platoon alignments, most notably with **Junior Caminero** (65.48) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (63.08). **Junior Caminero** overcomes a neutral park factor through strong order positioning and a favorable matchup profile, while **Kazuma Okamoto** leverages a +16% skill boost against the opposing starter, despite the lack of a finalized lineup. The most difficult decision of the day involved **Carson Benge** (50.02), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Carson Benge** provided a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher efficiency scores of **Luke Raley** and **Casey Schmitt**. We also remain cautious with **Christian Yelich** (54.64); though his platoon advantage is significant, his score is tempered by a negative park factor and an elite opposing catcher, requiring us to monitor his real-time output against Ashcraft closely to preserve our weekly game cap efficiency.",
